  "summary": "25+ years of experience in software design and development of high-performance image processing systems on UNIX and Windows platforms using C++, C#, Python, AI, and GPU frameworks. Extensive experience in GPU-accelerated image processing using CUDA, NPP, and custom CUDA kernel programming. Proven track record in deploying AI inference models for defect classification and object detection in semiconductor inspection systems.\n\nSkills:\n-------\n- Programming Languages: C++, C#, Python\n- Operating Systems: Unix, Windows\n- Database Management: MySQL, SQL Server\n- Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)\n- Real-Time Image Processing Systems: OpenCV, SIMD, NPP (NVIDIA Performance Primitives)\n- AI Frameworks: PyTorch, TensorFlow + Keras\n- GPU Image Processing: CUDA, CUDA Kernels, CUDnn, NPP\n- AI Inference Deployment: Defect classification, Object detection (Semiconductor inspection)\n- Docker / RabbitMQ\n\nProfessional Experience Highlights:\n- Designed and developed AI training and inference pipelines for deep learning models used in real-time defect classification and object detection within semiconductor and display manufacturing inspection systems.\n- Integrated NVIDIA NPP library and custom CUDA kernel programming for optimized 2D image processing and mathematical operations on GPU memory, achieving significant performance gains.\n- Implemented complex high-speed image processing algorithms with C++, CUDA, NPP, and OpenCV, optimizing for both Windows and Unix platforms.\n- Developed CUDA kernels using shared memory, stream synchronization, and occupancy optimization for tasks such as filtering, thresholding, histogram analysis, and ROI operations.\n- Deployed AI inference models (ONNX format) on production inspection systems using TensorRT and custom CUDA code, reducing inference latency and improving classification accuracy.\n- Led setup and tuning of GPU image processing servers using CUDA Toolkit (v12+), Nsight profiling tools, and Docker environments for scalable deployment.\n- Built integrated software systems that leverage RabbitMQ for asynchronous messaging between AI inference engines and user-facing labeling tools.\n- Supported real-time quality control processes by integrating AI inference with traditional image processing techniques for reliable inspection results.\n- Conducted performance profiling, code optimization, and memory management for large-scale image data pipelines and AI workloads.\n- Mentored junior developers on GPU programming paradigms, CUDA kernel structure, NPP usage, and AI model deployment best practices.",
